{"id":"a5","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":5,"of":10,"title":"Adjectives agree","titleHe":"שֵׁם תֹּאַר","goal":"Put an adjective after its noun and match it in gender, number and definiteness.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"An adjective comes after the noun it describes, not before, and it copies three things from it: gender, number, and whether it has the article."},{"type":"table","caption":"גָּדוֹל — big","head":["","singular","plural"],"rows":[["masculine","יֶלֶד גָּדוֹל","יְלָדִים גְּדוֹלִים"],["feminine","יַלְדָּה גְּדוֹלָה","יְלָדוֹת גְּדוֹלוֹת"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"If the noun takes the article, so does the adjective: הַיֶּלֶד הַגָּדוֹל, the big boy. Leave the second הַ off and you've written a whole sentence instead — הַיֶּלֶד גָּדוֹל means the boy is big."}],"vocab":[{"he":"גָּדוֹל","en":"big","translit":"gadol"},{"he":"קָטָן","en":"small","translit":"katan"},{"he":"טוֹב","en":"good","translit":"tov"},{"he":"רַע","en":"bad","translit":"ra"},{"he":"יָפֶה","en":"beautiful","translit":"yafe"},{"he":"חָדָשׁ","en":"new","translit":"chadash"},{"he":"יָשָׁן","en":"old (of things)","translit":"yashan"},{"he":"קָשֶׁה","en":"hard, difficult","translit":"kashe"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["city","he","hard, difficult","big"],"correct":3,"prompt":"גָּדוֹל","translit":"gadol"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["between","specifically, of all things","small","there"],"correct":2,"prompt":"קָטָן","translit":"katan"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["feeling","feels","his name","good"],"correct":3,"prompt":"טוֹב","translit":"tov"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["a little","woman","everything","bad"],"correct":3,"prompt":"רַע","translit":"ra"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["therefore","beautiful","hook","on me, about me"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יָפֶה","translit":"yafe"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["water","don't (with the future)","new","house"],"correct":2,"prompt":"חָדָשׁ","translit":"chadash"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["old (of things)","was born","house","dog"],"correct":0,"prompt":"יָשָׁן","translit":"yashan"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “new”?","options":["מִ","שֶׁלְּךָ","חָדָשׁ","נִגְמַר"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"What does הַיַּלְדָּה קְטַנָּה mean?","options":["The girl is small","The small girl","A small girl","The girl and the small one"],"correct":0,"why":"The adjective has no article, so this is a sentence, not a phrase."},{"type":"choice","q":"“The big house” is —","options":["הַבַּיִת הַגָּדוֹל","הַבַּיִת גָּדוֹל","בַּיִת הַגָּדוֹל","הַגָּדוֹל הַבַּיִת"],"correct":0,"why":"Both words take the article. Without the second one, הַבַּיִת גָּדוֹל, you've said the house is big."},{"type":"match","pairs":[["טוֹב","good"],["חָדָשׁ","new"],["קָשֶׁה","hard, difficult"],["יָשָׁן","old (of things)"],["קָטָן","small"]]},{"type":"read","he":"יָשָׁן","translit":"yashan","en":"old (of things)"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “big”?","options":["גָּדוֹל","עֵץ","יֵשׁ","מַעֲשֶׂה"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “beautiful”?","options":["וַיְהִי","גַּם","יָפֶה","בַּיִת"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “small”?","options":["מְדַבֵּר","קָטָן","שֶׁלִּי","לֶאֱכֹל"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["גָּדוֹל","יָפֶה","טוֹב","רַע"],"correct":1,"say":"יָפֶה","he":true}]}